ng the £260,000 Quilter PSO) ≈ £9,838.36, which matches arithmetically — but the report never states that the Quilter PSO is included in the charge basis, and it is excluded from the 'total transfer value' of £67,945.44. The report therefore states a fee and a percentage basis that cannot be reconciled without an assumption the report never makes. This is a material, self-contradicting figure that drives the cost disclosure and the recommendation. No 'as at' date or different basis guard applies: both figures are stated as contemporaneous. (2) MONTHLY EXPENDITURE — HIGH SEVERITY. The report states £2,986/month in the client situation section and £2,237/month in the cashflow modeller inputs — a £749/month (25%) difference. No explanation is given. The cashflow model uses the lower figure, which would materially affect the projected surplus/deficit output. This is a direct self-contradiction on a figure used in the modelling. (3) TRUE POTENTIAL CHARGE PRESENTATION — HIGH SEVERITY. The platform charge of 0.40% in the existing arrangements table and the 0.98% in the switch charges table are not in themselves contradictory — 0.98% = 0.40% platform + 0.58% fund management (+ 0.50% ongoing advice depending on inclusion). However, the like-for-like comparison uses 0.98% as the existing total and 0.39% as the new equivalent. The existing total of 0.98% includes the 0.50% ongoing advice charge; if the new 0.39% also excludes ongoing advice (1% new ongoing excluded), then the comparison is correctly like-for-like. But the report does not state this explicitly, and the 0.40% platform figure in the existing arrangements section appears to under-represent the total charge by 0.58% of fund charges. The inconsistency in how the figures are presented across sections without reconciliation is a disclosure and data consistency issue. (4) ONGOING SERVICE MONETARY FIGURE — HIGH SEVERITY. 1% of £67,945.44 = £679.45, which bears no resemblance to £3,181.08. The figure £3,181.08 is arithmetically consistent with 1% × (£327,945 − £9,838) ≈ £3,181, i.e. the combined fund value net of initial fee. However, the basis — that the ongoing charge is applied to all three arrangements including the PSO — is never stated. This is internally inconsistent and leaves the disclosed monetary amount unsupported by any stated calculation basis. (5) NEST RISK LEVEL FORMAT — LOW SEVERITY. The merged cell presentation for Nest ('Nest Higher Risk Fund 8') is a data quality / presentation issue creating ambiguity about whether '8' is a plan-level or fund-level risk rating. It does not contradict another stated figure but is an internal formatting inconsistency. The 'as at' date guard does not apply to any of these: all are contemporaneous figures within the same report. The basis guard applies partially to item (3) — the 0.40% and 0.98% are on different bases (platform only vs. total including fund charges and advice charge) — but the inconsistency in how the like-for-like table is presented is not fully resolved by this guard, because the report still uses 0.98% in one place and 0.40% in another without acknowledging the difference.","citations":[{"passageId":null,"source":"Canonical model — /costsAndCharges/initialAdviceCharge/monetaryAmount","category":"I","quote":"Initial fee stated as £9,838.36","cells":null},{"passageId":null,"source":"Canonical model — /solution/NP1/totalTransferValue","category":"I","quote":"Transfer value stated as £67,945.44","cells":null},{"passageId":null,"source":"Derived figures — charge arithmetic","category":null,"quote":"3% × £67,945.44 = £2,038.36","cells":null},{"passageId":null,"source":"Derived figures — total of all arrangements","category":null,"quote":"The 3 arrangements with a current value sum to £327,945.44","cells":null},{"passageId":null,"source":"Canonical model — /financialPosition/monthlyExpenditure","category":"I","quote":"£2,986 per month (current situation section)","cells":null},{"passageId":null,"source":"Canonical model — /cashflowModelling/inputs/monthlyExpenditure","category":"I","quote":"£2,237 per month (cashflow inputs)","cells":null},{"passageId":null,"source":"Canonical model — /existingArrangements/EA2/charges/platformCharge","category":"I","quote":"True Potential platform charge: 0.40% (existing arrangements table)","cells":null},{"passageId":null,"source":"Canonical model — /replacementAnalysis/EA2/existingAnnualCharge","category":"I","quote":"True Potential current annual recurring charge: 0.98% (switch charges table, includes ongoing advice of 0.50%)","cells":null},{"passageId":null,"source":"Canonical model — /ongoingService/annualCharge/percentage and /monetaryAmount","category":"I","quote":"Ongoing charge: 1% per annum; monetary equivalent: circa £3,181.08 for the first year","cells":null},{"passageId":null,"source":"Derived figures — NP1 total ongoing","category":null,"quote":"NP1 total ongoing: £1,278.99 at 0.39% implies a fund value of £327,946.15","cells":null}],"issueCategories":["Data inconsistency","Disclosure shortfall"],"severity":"High","outcome":"PotentialConcern"}

