ncy explicitly. No new capital is being committed from cash savings, so the emergency fund is not being directly depleted by the recommendation. However, the unexplained expenditure discrepancy in the cashflow modeller means the affordability and cashflow outputs may be unreliable, and the emergency fund is asserted as sufficient without evidenced quantification. These together constitute a Potential Concern at Moderate severity. No vulnerability characteristics are identified in the retrieved passages that materially alter this assessment.","citations":[{"passageId":"P5","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I","quote":"Your monthly expenditure totals £2,986 and Tony contributes £600 per month towards the household bills.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P4","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I","quote":"You earn £45,000 per ann","cells":null},{"passageId":"P2","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I","quote":"you have liquid cash should you require instance access funds.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P3","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I","quote":"Emergency funds","cells":["Emergency funds","£20,000"]}],"issueCategories":["Data inconsistency","Missing evidence","Weak justification"],"severity":"Moderate","outcome":"PotentialConcern"}

