tsheet [P2, P7] shows OCF of 0.63% for the UBS Aggressive fund. The SAP illustration [P6] shows Aviva AMC 0.25% pa with a 0.08% decrease applied (net 0.17%), fund costs of HSBC 0.21% and Vanguard 0.2207%, weighted average 0.2154%. The Aviva KFD [P13, P17] confirms charges are shown in the illustration and references adviser charges, DIM charges, and that fund charges are variable. No passage evidences the initial advice fee monetary amount of £9,838.36 as 3% of any explicitly stated combined transfer total. No passage states the basis for the ongoing adviser charge monetary figure of £3,181.08.","discrepancies":["1. The report states the initial advice fee is 3% giving a monetary amount of £9,838.36, but 3% of the stated transfer value of £67,945.44 (True Potential + Nest) = £2,038.36, not £9,838.36. The basis for £9,838.36 (implying a fund total of ~£327,945 including the Quilter PSO of £260,000) is never explicitly stated in the report, and no passage in the file reconciles this figure.","2. The report states the ongoing adviser charge is circa £3,181.08 for the first year, described as based on 'current values & expected contributions, minus the initial fee'. 1% of £67,945.44 = £679.45 (does not match). 1% of ~£327,945 minus £9,838 = ~£3,181 matches only if the Quilter PSO funds are included and the initial fee is deducted, but the report does not state this basis explicitly.","3. The SAP illustration [P6] shows Aviva AMC as 0.25% pa with a 0.08% decrease giving a net effective platform charge of 0.17%, whereas the report states 0.19% as the negotiated platform rate. These differ by 0.02pp; both are stated as Aviva's platform charge.","4. The SAP illustration [P6] shows fund weighted average ongoing cost of 0.2154%, whereas the Aviva illustration [P19] shows weighted average 0.20%, and the report states 0.20%. The SAP and illustration differ by 0.0154pp.","5. The report's annual recurring charges table includes only the ongoing product/platform/fund layers (0.39% total) and does not show the ongoing adviser charge (1%) in the same table, meaning no single row shows the all-in ongoing cost to the client.","6. The Quilter PSO (£260,000) is excluded from the pension switch charges comparison table without an explicit stated reason in the report (exclusion is inferred, not stated).","7. The True Potential existing arrangement platform charge is stated as 0.40% in the existing arrangements table, but the switch charges table uses 0.98% as the current annual recurring charge (inclusive of ongoing adviser charge of 0.50%). The like-for-like comparison subtracts the ongoing advice charge to produce a net comparable figure, but the basis for the 0.98% figure including the ongoing advice charge is used inconsistently across sections.","8. The report claims the ongoing service fee monetary equivalent is 'circa £3,181.08' but the stated basis ('current values & expected contributions, minus the initial fee') is not reconcilable with the stated transfer value of £67,945.44 alone — it is only reconcilable if the PSO funds are included, yet this is never stated."],"comparisonPerformed":true,"missingInputs":["Explicit statement in the report of the total fund value used as the basis for calculating the initial advice fee of £9,838.36 (i.e. whether the £260,000 Quilter PSO is included in the 3% calculation base).","Explicit statement of the basis for the ongoing adviser charge monetary figure of £3,181.08 (i.e. whether it is computed on the combined fund including Quilter PSO, net of the initial fee).","Reconciliation between the SAP platform charge (0.17% net after 0.08% discount from 0.25%) and the report's stated 0.19% negotiated rate."],"analysis":"The report discloses all required cost layers individually: platform (0.19%), investment management/fund (0.20%), initial adviser charge (3%), ongoing adviser charge (1%), and excludes transaction costs with a stated rationale that qualifies as a disclosure rather than a silent omission under the guard. The Aviva illustration [P18, P19] corroborates the platform charge at 0.19% and fund charges at a weighted average of 0.20%, and shows the cumulative effect of charges (all-charges RIY of 2.2% reduction in growth rate), satisfying the cumulativeEffectDisclosed assertion. The SAP tools [P5, P6] provide a comparative RIY of 1.5% for the Aviva solution.\n\nHowever, three material concerns remain after applying the guards:\n\nFirst, the initial advice fee monetary figure of £9,838.36 is arithmetically irreconcilable with the stated transfer value of £67,945.44 (3% × £67,945.44 = £2,038.36). It is only reconcilable if the Quilter PSO of £260,000 is included in the calculation base (3% × ~£327,945 ≈ £9,838), producing a combined total of approximately £327,945 — which matches the derived figures. However, the report never states this combined total as the basis for the fee. This is an internal inconsistency flagged by the extraction and confirmed by the derived figures: the report states 3% and £9,838.36 without stating the fund total to which 3% is applied. No passage in the file resolves this. This is a material disclosure shortfall: a client reading the report cannot verify the initial fee arithmetic from the information given.\n\nSecond, the ongoing adviser charge monetary figure of £3,181.08 is similarly only reconcilable against the full combined fund (£327,945 minus £9,838 initial fee ≈ £318,107 × 1% ≈ £3,181). The report's stated basis — 'current values & expected contributions, minus the initial fee' — does not make explicit that the Quilter PSO £260,000 is included. Again, no passage confirms the basis.\n\nThird, the annual recurring charges table (0.39%) does not include the ongoing adviser charge of 1%, so there is no single disclosed all-in ongoing charge figure. The report discloses them separately but never aggregates them. While the illustration [P18] captures all charges cumulatively, the report's own charges table is incomplete as a standalone disclosure.\n\nThe SAP platform charge discrepancy (0.17% vs 0.19%) is a minor difference likely attributable to rounding or the way the 0.08% discount from 0.25% is applied; the Aviva illustration [P19] directly confirms 0.19%, so this is low severity.\n\nThe Quilter PSO exclusion from the switch charges table is a genuine omission of explanation: the PSO is the largest asset being consolidated (£260,000 of £327,945 total) yet it does not appear in the like-for-like switch charges comparison. This affects the completeness of the comparison presented to the client.\n\nVulnerability overlay: No specific vulnerability characteristics are identified in the retrieved passages that would materially heighten the impact of these charge disclosure issues beyond the standard assessment.\n\nOn balance: the initial fee arithmetic is internally inconsistent and unreconciled in the report; the ongoing fee basis is unstated; no all-in ongoing percentage is disclosed in the charges table; and the largest asset is excluded from the switch charges comparison without stated reason. These collectively constitute material disclosure shortfalls requiring clarification.","citations":[{"passageId":"P8","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I","quote":"Platform 0.19%","cells":null},{"passageId":"P8","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I","quote":"Investment Management 0.20%","cells":null},{"passageId":"P8","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I","quote":"Total Charge 0.39%","cells":null},{"passageId":"P8","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I","quote":"£623.10","cells":null},{"passageId":"P8","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I","quote":"£655.89","cells":null},{"passageId":"P8","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I","quote":"The charges quoted in this report exclude the transaction costs of the underlying funds, as these are variable and subject to change based on factors such as market conditions and trad