{"groupId":"G7.5","requirement":"Benefit versus cost — fair value: where the report claims cost savings or justifies higher costs by reference to benefits, those claims must be consistent with and supported by the evidence in the case file.","reportSays":"The report asserts the following benefit/cost value claims: (1) Quilter platform charge 0.27% vs Aviva negotiated 0.19%, saving £208 p.a. (2) True Potential platform charge 0.40% vs Aviva 0.21%, saving 0.19% or £88.68 p.a. (3) True Potential fund charge 0.58% vs new plan 0.20%, saving £177.35 p.a. (4) Nest: new plan 0.39% vs existing 0.30%, small increase of £19.15 p.a. (5) Initial advice fee 3% = £9,838.36. (6) Ongoing service 1% p.a. = circa £3,181.08 for first year. (7) Qualitative benefits: investment flexibility, online platform access, flexible retirement options, ongoing monitoring. (8) The like-for-like switch analysis shows saving of 0.59% for True Potential (existing 0.98% vs new 0.39%). (9) The report does not state the basis for the £9,838.36 initial fee, nor the combined fund value (c.£327,945) on which both the initial fee and ongoing fee appear to be calculated.","fileSays":"The Selectapension switch analyses (P8, P9, P10, P11, P12, P14, P15) are in the case file. P11 (SAP All charges ex existing OAC) shows Aviva Pension Portfolio (Choice) AMC of 0.25% pa, reduced by 0.08% decrease, with fund charges of 0.2100% (HSBC) and 0.2207% (Vanguard), weighted average 0.2154%. P14 (SAP no charges ex existing OAC) shows projected inflation-adjusted values: Aviva £60,100/£151,000/£370,000 vs Existing £53,497/£134,613/£330,027 at 0%/2.94%/5.88% growth, RIY 0.4% for Aviva. P12/P15 (IAC only ex existing OAC) show True Potential transfer value £46,672.80 and Nest values. P10/P17 (All charges inc existing OAC) and P8/P9 provide fund performance data. The SAP analyses do not contain a figure for the Quilter/PSO platform charge of 0.27% to cross-reference the £208 saving. No provider illustration from Aviva is present in the retrieved passages that states negotiated platform rate of 0.19%. The derived figures confirm: 0.19% of £327,947 = £623.10 (consistent with negotiated rate applying to full combined fund); 0.21% of True Potential-only fund would be £97.89, not consistent with how the 0.21% is described; the True Potential fund saving of £88.68 at 0.19% of £46,672.80 = £88.68 (consistent). Nest increase of £19.15 at 0.09% of £21,272.64 = £19.15 (consistent). NP1 total ongoing 0.39% of £327,946 = £1,278.99. Ongoing 1% of (£327,945 − £9,838) ≈ £3,181 (broadly consistent if PSO included and initial fee deducted). The report states Aviva platform charge as both 0.19% (negotiated, vs Quilter 0.27%) and 0.21% (vs True Potential 0.40%) — these are two different figures for the same platform used in the same recommendation, without explanation. The SAP (P11) states AMC of 0.25% reduced by 0.08% = 0.17% net AMC, not 0.19% or 0.21%. The initial fee of £9,838.36 at 3% is arithmetically irreconcilable with the stated transfer value of £67,945.44 (which gives £2,038.36); it is consistent only with 3% of the full combined fund of ~£327,945 (including the Quilter PSO of £260,000), but the report never states this basis. No Aviva provider illustration is present in the evidence to confirm charges, projections or the negotiated rate.","discrepancies":["The report states the Aviva platform charge as 0.19% (when comparing against Quilter) and also as 0.21% (when comparing against True Potential) — two different figures for the same platform charge in the same recommendation, with no explanation of the difference.","The SAP analysis (P11) states the Aviva Pension Portfolio AMC as 0.25% reduced by a decrease of 0.08%, implying a net AMC of 0.17%, which matches neither the 0.19% nor the 0.21% figures stated in the report.","The initial advice fee of £9,838.36 is stated as 3% of the amount invested, but 3% of the stated transfer value of £67,945.44 = £2,038.36, not £9,838.36. The fee is consistent with 3% of ~£327,945 (full combined fund including PSO), but this basis is never stated in the report.","The ongoing fee of circa £3,181.08 at 1% p.a. is consistent with 1% of the combined fund net of initial fee (~£318,107), but 1% of the stated transfer value of £67,945.44 = only £679.45. The basis (full combined fund including PSO) is not stated.","No Aviva provider illustration is present in the evidence to corroborate the negotiated platform rate of 0.19%, the fund charges, or any projected values for the recommended plan.","The report claims a like-for-like saving of 0.59% on the True Potential switch (existing 0.98% vs new 0.39%), but the existing arrangements table shows True Potential platform charge as 0.40% and the switch table uses 0.98% (which includes the 0.50% ongoing advice charge), making the headline saving figure depend on whether ongoing advice is included on one side and not the other.","The Quilter PSO (EA1, £260,000) is absent from the Selectapension switch charges analysis, so no like-for-like charges comparison for the largest single arrangement is present in the evidence.","The report's description of the Aviva platform charge as 0.21% vs True Potential 0.40% giving a saving of 0.19% or £88.68: 0.19% × £46,672.80 = £88.68 (arithmetically correct), but 0.21% × £46,672.80 = £97.81, implying the saving calculation uses 0.19% not the difference between 0.21% and 0.40% (0.19%) — this is consistent only if the saving is 0.19 percentage points, which is the difference, so arithmetic is internally consistent, but the Aviva charge used (0.21%) differs from the 0.19% used elsewhere in the same section."],"comparisonPerformed":true,"missingInputs":["Aviva provider illustration confirming the negotiated platform rate (0.19% or 0.21%), fund charges and projected values","Quilter platform charge documentation confirming 0.27% to corroborate the £208 saving claim","Selectapension switch analysis covering the Quilter PSO arrangement (£260,000)","Explicit statement in the report of the basis for the £9,838.36 initial advice fee (i.e. that it is 3% of the full combined fund including PSO, not just the transfer value of £67,945.44)"],"analysis":"This requirement assesses whether the benefit-versus-cost claims in the report are consistent with and supported by the evidence. Several material issues arise.\n\n1. INCONSISTENT AVIVA PLATFORM CHARGE RATE: The report quotes the Aviva platform charge as 0.19% (when comparing against Quilter, saving £208 p.a.) and as 0.21% (when comparing against True Potential, saving £88.68). These are two different figures applied to the same recommended platform in the same section of the same report, with no explanation. The SAP analysis (P11) states the Aviva AMC as 0.25% reduced by 0.08%, implying 0.17% — matching neither figure. This is a data inconsistency that undermines the credibility of the cost-saving claims. The guard about different bases applies: the 0.19% may be a negotiated rate applicable to the full combined fund while 0.21% may be a different tier or a pre-negotiation rate, but the report never states this and neither does any evidence document.\n\n2. INITIAL ADVICE FEE BASIS UNDISCLOSED: The report states the initial advice fee is 3% of the amount invested = £9,838.36. The stated transfer value (True Potential + Nest only) is £67,945.44, giving 3% = £2,038.36. The fee of £9,838.36 is arithmetically consistent only with 3% of the full combined fund including the Quilter PSO (c.£327,945). The PSO funds are the largest single element. The report never states that the initial fee is calculated on the full combined fund including the PSO receipt. This is a disclosure shortfall: the client cannot verify the fee from the information given, and the basis for the largest cost item is opaque.\n\n3. ONGOING FEE BASIS: The ongoing fee of circa £3,181.08 at 1% is similarly consistent only with the full combined fund net of the initial fee. Again the basis is not stated. This is a lesser concern as the figure is broadly derivable, but it is not transparent.\n\n4. QUILTER PSO ABSENT FROM SWITCH ANALYSIS: The Quilter PSO (£260,000, the largest arrangement) is absent from the Selectapension switch charges analyses. No like-for-like charges comparison for this arrangement exists in the evidence. The report claims a cost saving of £208 p.a. on the Quilter platform charge (0.27% vs 0.19%), but this claim is unsupported by any corroborating document in the file. No Quilter KFD, illustration or charges schedule is present. The saving is asserted by the report alone, which is the assertion side, not the evidence side.\n\n5. NO AVIVA PROVIDER ILLUSTRATION: The SAP analyses are research/comparison tools. No formal Aviva provider illustration is present in the evidence confirming the negotiated rates, fund charges or projected values for the recommended plan. The SAP (P11) uses 0.25% AMC (−0.08% = 0.17% net), which does not match either the 0.19% or 0.21% quoted in the report. This means the key cost figures in the report have no independent corroboration.\n\n6. LIKE-FOR-LIKE COMPARISON ASYMMETRY: The switch analysis compares existing True Potential at 0.98% (including 0.50% ongoing advice charge) against new plan at 0.39% (excluding ongoing advice). The saving of 0.59% therefore partly reflects removal of the ongoing advice charge rather than a genuine product cost reduction. The report does acknowledge the like-for-like exclusion of ongoing advice in the charges table, but the presentation of the headline saving without making this adjustment explicit in the narrative is a disclosure shortfall.\n\n7. NEST COST INCREASE: The report correctly acknowledges that Nest costs increase by £19.15 p.a. (0.09% on £21,272.64) and provides a benefits rationale. The derived figures confirm this arithmetic. This element is adequately handled.\n\n8. VULNERABILITY: No specific vulnerability characteristics are identified in the evidence that would materially alter this assessment beyond the general need for clear disclosure.\n\nOverall: Multiple material discrepancies exist between the report's cost and benefit claims and the available evidence. The initial fee basis is arithmetically irreconcilable with the stated transfer value and is never explained. The platform charge rate is stated inconsistently within the same document. The largest arrangement (Quilter PSO, £260,000) has no corroborating charges documentation. These are not rounding differences; they go to the heart of whether the client can verify what they are paying and on what basis.","citations":[{"passageId":"P11","source":"Annes M SAP All charges ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":"Annual Management Charge: 0.25% pa","cells":null},{"passageId":"P11","source":"Annes M SAP All charges ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":"Decrease in Annual Management Charge of 0.08%","cells":null},{"passageId":"P11","source":"Annes M SAP All charges ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["HSBC Global Strategy Dynamic Portfolio Accumulation C","50.00%","0.0000%","0.2100%"]},{"passageId":"P11","source":"Annes M SAP All charges ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Vanguard LifeStrategy 80% Equity Fund A Acc","50.00%","0.0000%","0.2207%"]},{"passageId":"P11","source":"Annes M SAP All charges ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Weighted Average","","0.0000%","0.2154%"]},{"passageId":"P12","source":"Annes M SAP IAC only ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Fund Value at valuation date","£46,672.80"]},{"passageId":"P14","source":"Annes M SAP no charges ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Aviva","Pension Portfolio (Choice)","£60,100","£151,000","£370,000","0.4%"]},{"passageId":"P14","source":"Annes M SAP no charges ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Existing Plan","","£53,497.38","£134,612.81","