## Assumptions
The value of the investments in the Aviva Pension Portfolio (Choice) are based on medium level growth rate before charges are deducted.
As of 6th April 2006 (known as A-Day) every individual will be taxed on the amount by which they exceed their allowance. The allowance in the tax year 2021/22 for most individuals is £1.0731m. The allowance will index annually in line with Consumer Prices Index (CPI) from April 2026. Some individuals may have a higher allowance if they have registered for Protection (This is only relevant if you have a 'Protected Pension Commencement Lump Sum' in respect of the benefits accrued by the scheme before 6th April 2006).
## Death Benefit Comparison
On the day of switch, the capital value of the death benefits under your existing arrangements and the proposed replacement plan are as follows:
| True Potential Personal Pension   | £46,672   |
|-----------------------------------|-----------|
| nest Personal Pension             | £21,272   |
| Total                             | £67,945   |
| Aviva Pension Portfolio (Choice)  | £65,907   |
If the death benefit available after switch is lower than that provided by the existing arrangements, consideration should be given to replacing the shortfall.
A lump sum death benefit is available up to 100% of the fund. A tax charge may be levied on any amount above the Lifetime Limit Pension Commencement Lump Sum allowance.
After transfer - the proposed Aviva Pension Portfolio (Choice) will provide 97% of the existing plan's death benefit

