nfirmed at £46,672.80; Nest transfer value also confirmed in these documents. Aviva KFD confirms flexi-access drawdown available. True Potential Defaqto data confirms existing holdings performance. The switch analysis covers True Potential and Nest only; no equivalent switch analysis document is on file for the Quilter PSO (£260,000 — the largest single arrangement). The charge arithmetic derived figures confirm: Aviva platform charge 0.19% and investment management 0.20% applied to the total of all three arrangements (£327,947). The SAP documents show the recommended funds as HSBC Global Strategy Dynamic Portfolio Accumulation C (50%) and Vanguard LifeStrategy 80% Equity Fund A Acc (50%) with weighted average ongoing cost of 0.2154%.","discrepancies":["The Quilter PSO (£260,000 — the largest arrangement by value, representing ~79% of total funds) has no plan-specific switch charges analysis on file. The switch analysis documents cover only True Potential and Nest. This is the largest ceding plan with no cost/benefit analysis.","The 'All charges inc existing OAC' scenario (P17/P18) shows the existing schemes projected at £121,807 vs Aviva at £106,000 at 2.94% growth — i.e. the existing arrangements produce a better projected outcome on this basis. The report does not disclose or address the scenario in which the switch produces an inferior projected fund value compared to the existing arrangements.","The SAP analysis fund ongoing cost for the recommended funds shows a weighted average of 0.2154% (P5), whereas the report states investment management charge of 0.20%. These differ by 0.0154 percentage points (minor but present).","The switch analysis documents use a retirement age of 87 as the 'proposed age', but the report's canonical model does not explicitly state 87 as the client's target retirement age in the comparison section, creating a potential basis difference.","The Quilter PSO is included in the recommendation table and in the Aviva charge calculation (charge arithmetic confirms 0.19% applied to £327,947 — the total of all three arrangements) but is absent from the Pension Switch Charges Only Assessment table in the report and absent from all switch analysis documents.","The report asserts the Quilter platform charge is 0.27% conditional on retaining with Quilter, but no independent provider document corroborates this Quilter charge rate in the file.","The report states the True Potential like-for-like existing total is 0.98% and the saving is 0.59% (implying new = 0.39%). The existing arrangements table states True Potential platform charge as 0.40%, not 0.98%. The 0.98% includes ongoing advice charge of 0.50% and is used inconsistently (noted as an internal inconsistency in the extraction metadata)."],"comparisonPerformed":true,"missingInputs":[],"analysis":"The check covers whether each dimension the report compares is supported by provider or research documentation. Several material concerns arise.\n\n1. QUILTER PSO — NO SWITCH ANALYSIS: The largest arrangement (£260,000, ~79% of total funds) has no switch charges analysis on file and no plan-specific cost/benefit comparison. The SAP documents cover only True Potential and Nest. The severity guidance flags this as the highest severity situation: the largest ceding plan by value has no plan-specific cost/benefit analysis. No false-positive guard explains the absence of analysis for this plan; the PSO nature means it is being received rather than transferred out, but the charge calculation applied to it (Aviva 0.19% applied to the full £327,947 per the derived figures) means it is within scope of the ongoing cost comparison. Whether the switch of the Quilter plan is a voluntary transfer or a PSO receipt is itself ambiguous (noted in extraction ambiguities), but regardless the report justifies the platform charge saving of £208 p.a. against a Quilter 0.27% charge, and no Quilter provider document is on file to corroborate that charge rate.\n\n2. ADVERSE PROJECTION SCENARIO NOT DISCLOSED: The 'All charges inc existing OAC' SAP document (P17/P18) shows that when all charges including the existing ongoing advice charge are included, Aviva projects £106,000 vs existing £121,807 at 2.94% growth — the existing arrangements outperform Aviva. The report does not address or disclose this scenario. COBS 9.2.2R requires the report to present information that is fair, clear and not misleading. A scenario in which the existing arrangement produces a better projected outcome is material and its omission is a finding. The guard about different bases applies here: the 'all charges inc OAC' scenario incorporates the existing ongoing advice charge that the client would pay regardless, so the like-for-like comparison properly excludes it. However, the existence of the scenario where Aviva is worse should at minimum be acknowledged and explained, and it is not.\n\n3. CHARGES INCONSISTENCY — TRUE POTENTIAL: The 0.98% figure used in the like-for-like comparison includes the ongoing adviser charge of 0.50%, which inflates the apparent saving. The existing arrangements table states True Potential platform charge as 0.40%. The extraction metadata flags this as an internal inconsistency. The SAP 'ex existing OAC' documents appropriately exclude the existing OAC, but the report's narrative does not clearly explain what is included and excluded in the 0.98% vs 0.39% comparison.\n\n4. SUPPORTED DIMENSIONS: Flexi-access drawdown availability on Aviva is corroborated by the Aviva KFD (P10). The SAP 'ex existing OAC' and 'IAC only ex existing OAC' documents (P4/P15) show Aviva outperforming the existing arrangements on a like-for-like basis. Transfer values for True Potential and Nest are confirmed in the SAP documents. Investment pathways were considered and discounted (P1/P11). The fund range, risk alignment and adviser servicing claims are from the report itself ([I] passages) and have no independent corroboration in the file beyond the Aviva KFD confirming drawdown options.\n\n5. VULNERABILITY OVERLAY: No vulnerability-specific factors appear in the file that would materially alter this assessment.\n\nSummary: The primary concerns are (a) no switch analysis for the largest ceding plan (£260,000 Quilter PSO), (b) the adverse projection scenario (existing outperforms Aviva when all charges included) not being addressed in the report, and (c) the Quilter 0.27% charge claim having no independent documentary support. These are material gaps in the comparison.","citations":[{"passageId":"P2","source":"Annes M SAP All charges inc existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Fund Value at valuation date","£46,672.80"]},{"passageId":"P17","source":"Annes M SAP All charges inc existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Existing Plan","£48,408.31","£121,807.46","£298,632.72",""]},{"passageId":"P17","source":"Annes M SAP All charges inc existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Aviva","Pension Portfolio (Choice)","£42,300","£106,000","£261,000","1.5%"]},{"passageId":"P18","source":"Annes M SAP All charges inc existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Existing Schemes*","£48,408","£121,807","£298,632"]},{"passageId":"P18","source":"Annes M SAP All charges inc existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Aviva Pension Portfolio (Choice)","£42,300","£106,000","£261,000"]},{"passageId":"P14","source":"Annes M SAP no charges ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Existing Schemes*","£53,497","£134,612","£330,027"]},{"passageId":"P14","source":"Annes M SAP no charges ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Aviva Pension Portfolio (Choice)","£60,100","£151,000","£370,000"]},{"passageId":"P5","source":"Annes M SAP All charges ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["HSBC Global Strategy Dynamic Portfolio Accumulation C","50.00%","0.0000%","0.2100%"]},{"passageId