.94%, 6.32% at 5.88%) do not match those in the SAP documents (−0.6% at 1%, 2.33% at 2.94%, 5.25% at 5.88%). The growth rate assumptions in the SAP (1%, 2.94%, 5.88%) differ from those used in the report's critical yield table (0%, 2.94%, 5.88%). The £208 p.a. Quilter platform saving, the £19.15 Nest charge difference and the £275.37 True Potential saving are not corroborated by any passage. The PCLS comparison in P3 shows existing schemes £33,600 vs Aviva £26,600 (all charges scenario), while P7 shows existing £33,600 vs Aviva £36,600 (IAC only scenario).","discrepancies":["Critical yield at 0% growth: report states 0.41% (+0.41%); SAP documents show rate of return required at 1% growth of -0.60% (-0.60%) — different growth assumption and opposite sign (report's figure is not corroborated).","Critical yield at 2.94% growth: report states 3.37% (+0.43%); SAP 'all charges' shows 2.33% (-0.61%) at the same 2.94% growth rate — numerically inconsistent.","Critical yield at 5.88% growth: report states 6.32% (+0.44%); SAP 'all charges' shows 5.25% (-0.63%) at the same 5.88% growth rate — numerically inconsistent.","The sign convention differs: the report's critical yield figures are all positive (Aviva must outperform), whereas the SAP figures are all negative (Aviva needs to earn less to match existing), indicating a fundamentally different result or a different basis of comparison.","The SAP documents model True Potential and Nest only; the Quilter PSO is absent from every switch analysis document on file — no charges comparison, critical yield or cost/benefit analysis is evidenced for the largest single ceding plan by value (£260,000).","The report's stated £208 p.a. Quilter platform charge saving (0.08% difference) is not corroborated by any passage in the file.","The report's stated Nest charge difference of +0.09% / +£19.15 p.a. is not corroborated by any passage.","The report's stated True Potential like-for-like saving of -0.59% / -£275.37 p.a. is not corroborated by any passage.","The report states outperformance required vs Nest of 1.23% to age 89 at 2.94% growth; the SAP documents reference age 87 and show a negative rate of return required — inconsistent age and direction.","The PCLS comparison differs between SAP scenarios: P3 ('all charges') shows Aviva £26,600 vs existing £33,600 (Aviva lower); P7 ('IAC only') shows Aviva £36,600 vs existing £33,600 (Aviva higher) — these are scenarios not directly contradicting the report but show materially different outcomes depending on charge basis, and the report does not address the all-charges PCLS shortfall.","The SAP 'no charges' document (P8) uses plan charges of 0.4% monthly and fund AMC of 0.58%, not the negotiated 0.19% platform charge plus 0.20% fund charge stated in the report for Aviva — indicating the switch analysis documents may not reflect the actual negotiated rates."],"comparisonPerformed":true,"missingInputs":["Independent corroboration of the £208 p.a. Quilter platform saving figure","Switch analysis document for the Quilter PSO (largest ceding plan, £260,000)","Explanation of the basis difference between the report's critical yield figures and those in the SAP documents","Confirmation of which SAP scenario (all charges, IAC only, or no charges) was presented to the client as the primary comparison"],"analysis":"The report discloses switching costs and benefits for all three ceding plans and provides a critical yield table. However, there are material discrepancies between the report's critical yield figures and those in the SelectaPension analysis documents on file.\n\nFirst, and most significantly, the Quilter PSO — the largest ceding plan at £260,000, representing approximately 79% of the total fund being transferred — is absent from all three SelectaPension switch analysis documents. No plan-specific charges comparison, critical yield or cost/benefit analysis has been evidenced for this plan. The report relies solely on an assertion of a £208 p.a. saving from a 0.08% platform charge reduction, but this figure is uncorroborated by any file document. Under the severity guidance, the largest ceding plan by value lacking plan-specific cost/benefit analysis is a High concern.\n\nSecond, the critical yield figures in the report (0.41% at 0%, 3.37% at 2.94%, 6.32% at 5.88%) do not match those in the SAP 'all charges' documents (−0.60% at 1%, 2.33% at 2.94%, 5.25% at 5.88%). At the same 2.94% growth rate, the report states 3.37% required return while the SAP shows 2.33%. At 5.88%, the report states 6.32% while the SAP shows 5.25%. The sign reversal is also significant: the report shows positive figures (Aviva must outperform to match existing), while the SAP shows negative figures (Aviva needs lower returns to match existing), suggesting either a different basis of calculation or that the critical yield table in the report relates to a combined scenario (including PSO) not modelled in the SAP documents. The SAP 'no charges' document (P8) shows the plan charges used as 0.4% monthly and fund AMC of 0.58%, not the negotiated 0.17% Aviva platform plus 0.20% fund charge stated in the recommendation — this may explain part of the discrepancy but is not reconciled in the report.\n\nThird, the Nest charge difference (£19.15 p.a.) and the True Potential saving (£275.37 p.a.) stated in the switch charges table are not independently corroborated in any passage, though the SAP does cover these two plans.\n\nThe guard on non-financial benefits applies: the report argues adviser servicing, wider fund range and drawdown flexibility explicitly, which can justify the small Nest cost increase (£19.15 p.a.). However, this guard does not remedy the absence of any switch analysis for the Quilter PSO or the contradiction between the report's critical yield figures and those in the SAP.\n\nThe vulnerability overlay: the extraction notes absence of vulnerability detail, so no additional finding arises here.\n\nOverall: the Quilter PSO lacks any evidenced switch analysis (High); the critical yield figures in the report contradict those in the SAP documents (High); the monetary charge savings for all three plans are unconfirmed by independent evidence.","citations":[{"passageId":"P1","source":"Annes M SAP no charges ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Rate of Return Required from Aviva","1%: -0.6% (-0.6%)","2.94%: 2.33% (-0.61%)","5.88%: 5.25% (-0.63%)"]},{"passageId":"P1","source":"Annes M SAP no charges ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":"The projections have been system generated using 0.4% plan charges monthly, 0.58% Fund AMC.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P4","source":"Annes M SAP All charges ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["True Potential Personal Pension","Fund Value at valuation date","£46,672.80","Transfer Value at valuation date","£46,672.80"]},{"passageId":"P8","source":"Annes M SAP no charges ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Aviva","Pension Portfolio (Choice)","£60,100","£151,000","£370,000","0.4%","Existing Plan","£53,497.38","£134,612.81","£330,027.33"]},{"passageId":"P3","source":"Annes M SAP All charges ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Existing Schemes","£33,600","Aviva Pension Portfolio (Choice)","£26,600"]},{"passageId":"P7","source":"Annes M SAP IAC only ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Existing Schemes","£33,600","Aviva Pension Portfolio (Choice)","£36,600"]},{"passageId":"P5","source":"Annes M SAP All charges ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":"Annual Management Charge: 0.25% pa","cells":null},{"passageId":"P5","source":"Annes M SAP All charges ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":"Decrease in Annual Management Charge of 0.08%","cells":null}],"issueCategories":["Missing evidence","Data inconsistency","Weak justification","Compliance concern"],"severity":"High","outcome":"PotentialConcern